# Code owners — DELIBERATELY NOT a global rule.
#
# `* @GabinSMD` used to sit at the top. With a single maintainer and no branch
# requiring reviews (develop, staging and master all have
# required_pull_request_reviews disabled), it honoured nothing and requested a
# review on every pull request — 26 of 50 unread notifications at the time this
# was narrowed, Dependabot included.
#
# What remains covers the paths where an unreviewed change actually hurts, so
# the file is ready the day required code-owner reviews are switched on — which
# the public repository makes plausible once outside contributions arrive.
# Until then these requests stay rare, because these paths rarely move.

# Security-critical
apps/backend/src/auth/          @GabinSMD
apps/backend/src/payment/       @GabinSMD
apps/backend/src/main.ts        @GabinSMD

# Data model: migrations run on container start and deploys roll back on failure
apps/backend/prisma/            @GabinSMD

# Infrastructure & secrets
infra/                          @GabinSMD
.github/workflows/              @GabinSMD

# Mobile release identity: a mistake here ships to the stores
apps/client/app.config.js       @GabinSMD
apps/client/eas.json            @GabinSMD
